  "id": "d2a3d46f-af48-50e6-a0bb-a30528484ddc",
  "slug": "frozen-tiramisu",
  "name": "Frozen Tiramisu",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "Love tiramisu but don't have time to make it? My ice cream version rivals the real thing and can be prepared in under half an hour, no pastry skills required - not a bad return on a dessert that serves up to 14 people.",
  "cuisine": null,
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Mix coffee and rum. Line a 2-quart metal loaf pan with plastic wrap, leaving an overhang. Use a pastry brush to paint the spiked coffee onto the ladyfingers. Then line the bottom and sides of the pan with ladyfingers, rounded side out."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Reserving 1/2 cup of chocolate for garnish, stir rest of chocolate into ice cream. Turn ice cream into loaf pan, using a rubber spatula to press ice cream evenly into pan. Cover with plastic wrap and freeze for at least 2 hours or up to 5 days."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "When ready to serve, mix cheese, liqueur and sugar until smooth; whisk in half-and-half to form a thick but pourable sauce. Unmold dessert, using ends of plastic wrap to remove it from pan; peel away wrap. Slice loaf, drizzle with sauce and sprinkle with chocolate."
    }
  ],
